error[E0818]: `"x86-interrupt"` is not an ABI wolf has — the only one is `"c"`
 --> mem:///main.lu:1:8
  |
1 | extern "x86-interrupt" fn isr() {
  |        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ unknown ABI
  |
  = note: `[abi.c.seams]`: the one ABI string is `"c"`. An interrupt or exception handler is
    entered through an assembly trampoline that saves the registers, calls an `export fn`
    with the C convention, and returns with `iretq` (KWC F7, K7); a function written with
    another ABI string would compile as an ordinary function and return with `ret`.
